WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:01.680
BUKOLA AYODELE:
Today, we're talking

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:05.250
about user-friendly SQL, Cloud
Scheduler, and cybersecurity

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:06.180
in health care.

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:06.960
I'm Bukola.

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:08.400
And welcome to
this week in cloud,

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:11.720
where we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:15.110
We're expanding BigQuery's
commitment to user-friendly SQL

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:18.020
through a whole slew
of new SQL features.

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:20.900
From expanded SQL expressions
and scripting control

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:24.170
statements to expanded data
types and information schema

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:27.560
views, we're making BigQuery
easier for you to use.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:30.560
Check out the blog for more.

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:32.900
Reliably executing
tasks on schedule

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:34.700
is critical for
everything from data

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:37.580
engineering to infrastructure
management and application

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:38.540
maintenance.

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:40.250
Today, we are
thrilled to announce

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:43.040
that Google Cloud Scheduler,
our enterprise-grade scheduling

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:46.920
service, is now available
in more GCP regions.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:49.010
In addition, multiple
regions can now

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:52.430
be used from a single project,
removing the prior limits

00:00:52.430 --> 00:00:55.650
of a single region per project.

00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:58.320
With all the crises that
have buffeted the health care

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:01.260
and life science industries
over the past few years,

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:04.440
one that often gets overlooked
is the unceasing wave

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:08.820
of cyber attacks aimed at
medical, research, educational,

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:11.070
and public health organizations.

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:13.710
The best way to put an end
to these persistent threats

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:16.530
to improve the resilience of
health care organizations'

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:19.440
IT systems, they
might do well to look

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:21.390
at their own industry
for inspiration

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:24.120
and an approach akin
to exposure therapy.

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:27.020
Check out the blog
for more details.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:29.150
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:32.070
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:35.220
Any thoughts or ideas, leave
us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:37.390
We'll see you in the cloud.

